# UI preview reminder (react-spectrum-demo)

When your changes affect **user-visible UI** (React Spectrum components, Spectrum CSS, Storybook stories, chromatic stories, or MDX examples), end the same response with a short **Preview** block so the user can run Storybook and open it from Cursor.

Use this repo’s defaults unless `package.json` scripts differ:

**Main Storybook (v3 / default `yarn start`):**

```bash
yarn start
```

**Local URL (clickable in Cursor):** [http://localhost:9003](http://localhost:9003)

**S2 Storybook** (only if the change is under S2 / `.storybook-s2`):

```bash
yarn start:s2
```

**Local URL:** [http://localhost:6006](http://localhost:6006)

Rules:

- Print the **exact** `yarn` line from this project (`yarn start` or `yarn start:s2`), not a paraphrase.
- Always use the full `http://localhost:…` link (with port) so it is clickable in the chat UI.
- If Storybook is already running, still include the link; mention they can refresh if the dev server is up.
- Skip this block only when the change is purely non-UI (types-only, tests without stories, tooling, docs with no live examples).
